codemap 8
path gui-structure
kind layer
author ai
group gui
note How the gui crate is divided and the rules each part keeps. The App is what platform calls - once per frame, once per script line - and it owns four things: the Model, which is all the state a view can see (index, map, selection, panel state, fields, server questions, status); the Services, the threads and the channels to them, which no view sees; the Ui element tree; and the cache of drawn code grids. The rules: views (views.rs and views/) take &Model and push Actions onto the Frame's queue, and never change anything; apply is the one place state changes - it runs the keys' and dock's actions before the tree is built and the queue after it; nav.rs owns the selection, whose fields no other module can write; runtime.rs owns threads, since every background job and service is started there and the lint that forbids thread::spawn is lifted only there; work.rs sends questions to the threads and folds their answers into the Model at the top of the frame; widgets are Frame methods that take their sizes and colours from theme and name their elements through ids; keys decides which chord, click or wheel means what, from the feature registry, so no view tests a modifier itself; status.rs words everything the status line and the output log say; dump.rs prints what a script's dump asks, each part of the Model through the Dump trait. The one exception to 'nothing changes outside apply' is the Frame's Overlay, which carries what a view decided this frame to the views drawn after it.

